{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1684","id":5146882765,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUoK9js8AAAABMscyzQ","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1684","diff_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1684.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1684.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1684","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1684/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1684/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1684/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/statuses/ba7d4bd8b1295098d458e67d7647674d61160870","number":1684,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"T-2376: the Green Tree shoulder light gets its pointed gable cap","user":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nOne bounded, data-only trial inside the still-open original picture case **T-2376**\n(*Match the Green Tree Tavern to its pictures*). The only geometric data change is\n\n```\nphases.frame_1833.form.enclosed_left_annex.value.shoulder.front_gable_peak_m\n  4.50 m  ->  4.85 m\n```\n\nso the small front-gable light over the Green Tree's enclosed shoulder reads as the\nsharply pointed cap Andreas's detailed retrospective engraving draws, instead of the\nblunt, nearly flat one the earlier value produced.\n\n## Why\n\nThe builder sets the dormer wall head from the light itself (3.35 m sill + 0.70 m\nheight + 0.15 m head margin = 4.20 m) over a roof half-span of (0.65 m light + 0.50 m\ncheeks + 0.10 m overhang) / 2 = 0.625 m. A 4.50 m peak over that is a cap of about\n**25.6°**; 4.85 m gives about **46.1°** and the pointed shape the picture shows. The\nclapboard courses step up the little gable face with it.\n\n**4.85 m is a RECONSTRUCTED working control for the drawn shape, not a measurement.**\nThe plate carries no scale, no dimension, no geographic camera and no date, so nothing\nhere is measured and nothing is dated. Confidence on `enclosed_left_annex` stays\n`reconstructed`; recorded in `docs/LIBERTIES.md`\n§ `L-green-tree-shoulder-dormer-cap-2376`.\n\n## The build\n\nBuilt on the pinned Blender 4.5.3 (`generators/blender.pin`, sha-verified cache), never\nhand-edited. `validate.py --stale` named exactly one stale master and exactly one was\nrebuilt:\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| inputs_sha256 | `80d47de6a302…` | `bb16568756e3…` |\n| MASTER `assets/gltf/green_tree_tavern__frame_1833.glb` | `0b53a6fe…` (269,880 B) | `f213818f…` (270,816 B) |\n| WEB `assets/web/green_tree_tavern__frame_1833.glb` | `0154cfad…` (48,648 B) | `65863b3c…` (48,772 B) |\n\nThe WEB derivative was encoded in the same run from the new master; the old one is not\nrelabelled. Every other row of `assets/manifest.json` and `assets/manifest.web.json` is\nuntouched, and no foreign registry entry or producer family is involved — the three\nactive jobs (Jail/`frame_dwelling`, first fort/`outbuilding`, second fort/`fort_structure`)\nare not touched. No producer, parameter-validator, schema or recipe-scheme was edited.\n\n### Containment, measured on the exported meshes\n\n- triangles **3,318 → 3,330** (+12)\n- the two dormer **ridge vertices raised 0.35 m** (y 4.50 → 4.85 at x 9.42, z −12.71 / −11.71)\n- **24 cladding vertices added** in the 4.307–4.581 m band — the gable-course infill\n- **every other primitive byte-identical** (occupied rings, door faces, ground, entry,\n  main block, chimneys, glass elsewhere)\n- **full model bounding box exactly equal**: `[-0.25, 0.0, -15.131628] … [18.177464, 8.722019, 0.355]`\n- the peak stays below the unchanged 5.0 m main-block wall head and far below the model's\n  existing 8.722 m maximum\n\n## Before / after\n\nControlled: the **same camera** (`9439f5f7…`) and the **same picture** (`bfaa184f…`),\nonly the master rebuilt.\n\n- before — `docs/RESEARCH/green-tree-annex-T-2376/andreas_1838-side-by-side-before-dormer-cap-20261104.jpg` (preserved by this PR)\n- after — `docs/RESEARCH/photo-match/green_tree_tavern/andreas_1838-side-by-side.jpg`\n\nThe side-by-side was reviewed directly. The sharper cap reads as the pictured pointed\nlight; no sky seam, hole or roof penetration appears. The closed shoulder, its lower\nsash and upper light, and the two separate uncovered farm wagons are retained — no\nshed, posts or covered wagon returns.\n\n## What this does NOT claim\n\n`data/reference_views/green_tree_tavern/andreas_1838.match.json` stays **`differs`**.\nThe old compound OPEN row is split truthfully: only the sharper dormer cap is marked\n`fixed`; a row stays **OPEN** for the shoulder's own roof slope and eaves line and for\nthe relative proportions of shoulder, connector and turned range against the main block.\n\n- Trowbridge/Gale 1902 (retrospectively captioned 1835) shows an **open** post-and-roof\n  wagon bay against the chosen enclosed shoulder. That source disagreement and the\n  unknown conversion date remain explicit; nothing here dates the change to 1 July 1835.\n- Andreas is verified public-domain **1884** and retrospective; the familiar\n  \"INN–1838\" caption is not an independently established date, dimension or camera.\n- The upper/attic opening-count disagreement between the drawings and the retained\n  camera/pixel residuals stay **within tolerance** (T-3153). No new calibration barrier\n  and no photo follow-up ticket.\n- `chm_green_tree_1859` stays unverified / `check_required` / link-only: no derivative\n  retrieved, no geometry derived, no spot. All four credited picture rows are preserved.\n- The original's wider coverage — Andreas 1884, Trowbridge/Gale 1902, CHM c1859, Kurz &\n  Allison 1893, plus both named reproductions — is **still incomplete**. **T-2376 stays\n  open / partial / differs**; no signoff, no `done --anyway`, no split, no new ticket.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `./tools/check.sh --part 1/4` … `4/4`, each a bounded foreground call: **all four PASS**,\n  0 red of 287 / 287 / 288 / 286 steps. No step reported a missing module, so none was\n  skipped. (Part 3 first failed on `data/liberties.json` not matching the appended\n  `LIBERTIES.md`; `tools/compile_liberties.py` was re-run and part 3 re-run green. Parts\n  1, 2 and 4 ran before that regeneration — the hosted gate re-proves the whole tree on\n  this head.)\n- `tools/bake.sh --only green_tree_tavern` on the pinned Blender; master + web derivative\n  written by that run.\n- `node tools/photo_match.mjs data/reference_views/green_tree_tavern/andreas_1838.json`\n  at the unchanged camera and picture.\n- Smoke by parts per `node tools/smoke_budget.mjs --for-diff`, plus desktop 1280×800 and\n  phone 390×780 review of the building in the published app — recorded in a comment below.\n\n## Docs\n\n`docs/LIBERTIES.md` (new bounded entry, appended — the book is not replaced),\n`data/liberties.json` recompiled, `docs/STATUS.md` and\n`docs/RESEARCH/green-tree-annex-T-2376/README.md` appended without replacing any\nexisting section, and one visitor-facing What's-New entry in `changelog.d/T-2376.json`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T00:47:12Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T00:56:00Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kevinrhaas:steward/t2376-dormer-peak-native-20261104","ref":"steward/t2376-dormer-peak-native-20261104","repo":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":null,"homepage":null,"language":"Python","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"watchers":0,"open_issues_count":11,"open_issues":11,"size":14418559,"default_branch